    "safety_settings": null,
    "tools_declarations": null,
    "function_call_request": null,
    "response_text": "Idempotency keys let a client safely retry the same request and guarantee the server returns the same result without performing the action twice. Deduplication is a broader server-side technique to detect and suppress duplicates that may not share an explicit key. Idempotency is usually scoped to a single endpoint and time window and is opt-in per request. Dedup often relies on heuristics (payload hashes, timestamps, actor) and can be lossy. Payment APIs typically prefer explicit idempotency keys for correctness and auditability.",
    "response_raw": {
