    "response_text": "SSE is simpler for one-way token streams: HTTP-friendly, easy with proxies/CDNs, auto-reconnect, and works well with auth cookies. WebSockets support bidirectional messaging and lower overhead for frequent client → server events, but are trickier through some intermediaries and require more lifecycle handling. If you mainly stream tokens and send occasional user messages via regular HTTP, SSE is often the pragmatic choice; use WebSockets when you need real-time duplex control (interrupt, tool events, shared cursors).",
